  <!-- Structured Data - FAQ for Featured Snippets -->
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Can I use SERP API for free?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes, up to a point. Serpent API gives every new account free calls shared across every endpoint, with no credit card. Serper gives 2,500 free queries, Bright Data 5,000 a month, Oxylabs 2,000 results, SerpApi 250 searches a month and Scrapingdog 200 credits, which is about 40 Google searches. No SERP API is free forever at production volume, because every provider pays real infrastructure cost on each request. Free tiers are for evaluation, so the question that matters is what the first paid call costs. For context on the paid side: at our Scale rate, Bright Data's entire 5,000-search monthly free tier would cost you 50 cents on Scale, or 15 cents on Enterprise."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Which API is the cheapest?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "By published rates read on 10 September 2026, Serpent API is the cheapest SERP API at $0.03 per 1,000 calls on the Enterprise tier, reached with one $1,000 deposit. Ranked by the best rate each vendor publishes, the rest run Scrapingdog $0.14, Serper $0.30, Oxylabs $0.50, DataForSEO $0.60, Bright Data $1.30 and SerpApi $1.96. Those floors are not equally reachable, though. Oxylabs' $0.50 sits on a quote-only Custom+ tier, Serper's $0.30 needs a $3,750 credit purchase and SerpApi's $1.96 a $106,050 plan, so compare entry prices too if you are not yet at that volume."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How expensive is SERP API?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "It depends on the vendor and the unit. Entry prices across the six providers we track run from $0.60 to $25.00 per 1,000 searches. Serpent API starts at $0.60 per 1,000 Web units on Default. Paid credit starts with a $10 minimum deposit; after lifetime deposits reach $50, further top-ups have a $100 minimum. The Web rate drops to $0.30 after a one-time $100 deposit and to $0.10 after a one-time $500 deposit, or $0.03 after a one-time $1,000 Enterprise deposit. Existing credit keeps its original price schedule, while new deposits use the current schedule; deposited credit does not expire. Refunded or charged-back amounts don't count toward your tier. Watch the unit as well as the price: on Deep Search a page of 10 results is the unit, so 100 results costs ten times a single-page call. A worked example at one million single-page searches a month. That is $100 on our Scale tier or $30 on our Enterprise tier; for 10-page Deep requests targeting up to 100 results each, it is $1,000 on Scale or $300 on Enterprise. Serper's largest pack rate allocates $300 of credit use per month after a $3,750 pack purchase; SerpApi's Cloud 1M monthly plan bills $3,750."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Is there a free version of Serper?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Serper offers 2,500 free queries with no credit card required, which is one of the larger free tiers in this category. After that it sells prepaid credit packs running from about $1.00 per 1,000 queries down to $0.30 per 1,000 on the 12.5 million credit pack, and credits expire six months after purchase. Serper publishes no AI Overview endpoint. If you need AI Overview data or a rate below $0.30, free tier size is not the number to compare on. Prices and free tiers on this page were last verified on 10 September 2026."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is Serpent API?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Serpent API provides search results from Google, Bing, Yahoo, DuckDuckGo and Brave, AI mention tracking across ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Perplexity, plus YouTube, Instagram and LinkedIn data APIs. All in one platform with simple JSON responses."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Is Serpent API free?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Every new account gets shared free calls on eligible endpoints. No credit card required. After that, web is $0.60/1K Web units Default, $0.30/1K units with one $100 deposit, or $0.10/1K units with a one-time $500 deposit, or $0.03/1K units with a one-time $1,000 Enterprise deposit (20× off) — with one Web unit per Quick call and one per requested Deep page."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How much does Serpent API cost?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Pay-as-you-go pricing. Web requests are $0.60/1K Default, $0.30/1K with one $100 deposit, or $0.10/1K with a one-time $500 deposit, or $0.03/1K with a one-time $1,000 Enterprise deposit. News is $0.20/$0.02/$0.01 per 1K, Images are $0.35/$0.32/$0.25 per 1K, and Videos are $0.10/$0.09/$0.07 per 1K. New accounts get shared free calls on eligible endpoints."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Which search engines are supported?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Serpent API supports five search engines: Google (default), Bing, Yahoo, DuckDuckGo, and Brave. You can choose which search engine to use for each API request using a simple engine parameter. Access web, news, and image search results from all five search engines through a single unified API."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How do I get started?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Getting started is easy: 1) Sign up with your Google account, 2) Get your API key from the dashboard, 3) Start making API requests. You will receive shared free calls on eligible endpoints upon registration -- no credit card required."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How many search results can I get per query?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Serpent API returns up to 100 organic search results per query, along with related searches, People Also Ask questions, and featured snippets when available."
        }
      }
    ]
  }
  </script>

  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" crossorigin>
